description:
@resonance/core owns EMBEDDING_DIMS (1024) plus assertEmbeddingDims / EmbeddingDimensionError (added by resonance-6762, ADR-0010).

DB HALF DONE (2026-07-26, seed resonance-663d): packages/db/src/schema/creator.ts now uses `vector("embedding", { dimensions: EMBEDDING_DIMS })` imported from @resonance/core instead of the literal 1024. Verified non-churning: drizzle-kit reported 'no schema changes, nothing to migrate' and every migration file's SHA-256 was unchanged.

REMAINING (packages/ai only): packages/ai/src/embeddings.ts still declares its own EMBEDDING_DIMS (re-exported from ai's index.ts) and hand-rolls its dimension check in embedVoyage. Re-export core's value rather than declaring a second one, and replace the hand-rolled check with assertEmbeddingDims — noting that today it throws AgentError, so decide deliberately whether callers should now see EmbeddingDimensionError (a ResonanceError subclass) and update ai's tests accordingly.
